What's the villains' side called?

286
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:53,960
Decepticons.

287
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:55,280
See? Didn't someone mention Decepticons...

288
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:56,440
Isn't there a character named Decepticons?

289
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:58,480
He said Decepticons was an individual character.

290
00:10:58,480 --> 00:11:00,640
I remembered it as an individual too.

291
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:03,280
In Transformers, is there...

292
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:05,040
a character called Decepticons?

293
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:07,680
You're right, you're right.

294
00:11:07,680 --> 00:11:08,920
Xiao Hu is right.

295
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:09,640
There isn't.

296
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:10,880
There's no character called Decepticons.

297
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:11,920
There's only...

298
00:11:11,920 --> 00:11:13,360
Its leader is Megatron.

299
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:14,720
The faction is called Decepticons.

300
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:17,520
Give it up for Xiao Hu!

301
00:11:19,040 --> 00:11:20,480
The other guy is Optimus Prime.

302
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:23,280
What's Optimus Prime's faction called?

303
00:11:23,280 --> 00:11:24,520
That faction is the Autobots.

304
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:25,480
It's the Autobots.

305
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:28,320
Aren't they all called Autobots?

306
00:11:29,840 --> 00:11:31,280
Are Decepticons called Autobots too?

307
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:32,360
Aren't they all Autobots?

308
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:34,120
Aren't some of them made from planes?

309
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:35,840
Are Decepticons Autobots?

310
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:37,360
Autobots is also a faction!

311
00:11:37,520 --> 00:11:39,080
What are the good guys called?

312
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:39,920
Autobots.

313
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:41,560
Look, he laid everything out...

314
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:43,120
crystal clear for you!

315
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:49,760
On a plateau, the key is doing everything slowly.

316
00:11:49,760 --> 00:11:51,320
The first time I went up to a plateau,

317
00:11:51,320 --> 00:11:52,280
I was super excited.

318
00:11:52,280 --> 00:11:53,520
Then I spotted a butterfly,

319
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:54,880
and dashed over to catch it.

320
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:57,200
Suddenly, my mind went completely blank.

321
00:11:57,720 --> 00:11:58,880
I collapsed right there.

322
00:11:58,880 --> 00:12:00,800
I mean, you ran out of oxygen!

323
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:03,680
Isn't Jade Dragon Snow Mountain 4,680 meters?

324
00:12:03,680 --> 00:12:04,520
Yeah.

325
00:12:04,520 --> 00:12:05,440
The highest point here is around that too.

326
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:06,120
The entire region...

327
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:08,440
The Western Sichuan Plateau is over 4,000 meters too.

328
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:10,560
Like Aba Prefecture, it's all over 4,000 meters.

329
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:12,360
When I was heading downhill at Jade Dragon Snow Mountain,

330
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:13,120
I was still...

331
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:14,240
bouncing around!

332
00:12:14,240 --> 00:12:15,800
Really? You were completely fine?

333
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:17,200
I collapsed the second I reached the hotel.

334
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:20,320
Felt completely fine while I was up there.

335
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:21,360
If you managed to make it to the hotel,

336
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:22,720
that's already pretty solid.

337
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:24,360
Later, I built up stamina so at over 5,000 meters,

338
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:25,560
I could still join the locals

339
00:12:25,560 --> 00:12:27,280
for a high-altitude basketball game!

340
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:28,360
A high-altitude basketball game?

341
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:29,040
Today?

342
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:31,120
Now you're speaking Anyu's language!

343
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:32,440
His competitive drive is fired up!

344
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:33,560
Now I'm wide awake!

345
00:12:33,760 --> 00:12:34,840
Tossed away my cane,

346
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:37,400
don't need glucose anymore!

347
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:39,000
That's my thing—I played basketball in high school!

348
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:50,640
Look at these huge rocks.

349
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,520
Can anyone tell me why

350
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:54,600
plants don't grow on some of them?

351
00:12:55,320 --> 00:12:56,120
Chen,

352
00:12:56,560 --> 00:12:59,480
he's asking why plants don't grow on some rocks.

353
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:01,800
Because a lot of them were

354
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:04,120
eroded by glaciers.

355
00:13:04,120 --> 00:13:06,400
The soil here is generally very soft,

356
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:08,160
and there were landslides.

357
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:09,680
Because there were earthquakes here.

358
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:10,880
Every time an earthquake hit,

359
00:13:10,880 --> 00:13:13,080
it accelerated all the soil erosion here.

360
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:14,720
So the spots where you see no plants

361
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:16,320
are all marks left after earthquakes,

362
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:18,320
where the soil slid down.

363
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:20,320
It's even more obvious in Xinjiang.

364
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:21,440
In Xinjiang, plants don't grow—

365
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:23,440
they only grow in the ravines,

366
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:24,360
because there's moisture.

367
00:13:24,640 --> 00:13:27,440
Nothing grows at all where there's no moisture.

368
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:30,600
And the high-altitude plants are all spruces.

369
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:32,680
Spruces are a type of fir,

370
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:34,040
which are gymnosperms.

371
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:54,240
Let me spar with him.

372
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:55,040
Go ahead, you spar.

373
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:58,040
Go easy grappling us.

374
00:13:58,640 --> 00:14:00,200
Six of us can't beat one guy?

375
00:14:02,680 --> 00:14:04,400
Don't go for Officer Huang's lower body.

376
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:05,960
He can't do anything to your upper body.

377
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:07,880
Once he wraps his legs around you, you're done.

378
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:08,960
I'll take his right leg.

379
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:11,120
Going for his dominant leg, huh?

380
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:13,120
That's brave.

381
00:14:13,320 --> 00:14:15,080
I'll lock down his tonsils.

382
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:16,320
I'll hit him with Dahong Fist.

383
00:14:18,840 --> 00:14:21,240
I'll use my neck to hard-lock his hand.

384
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:23,960
So you're just letting him choke you?

385
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:29,280
How many flights of stairs...

386
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:29,880
...are left?

387
00:14:30,440 --> 00:14:33,160
Officer Huang, have some glucose.

388
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:34,080
It really works.

389
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:35,200
It's way too sweet.

390
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:37,640
Your muscles consume too much oxygen.

391
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:38,400
Right.

392
00:14:38,760 --> 00:14:40,640
That's why we need to train them...

393
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:41,360
...to use less oxygen.

394
00:14:42,720 --> 00:14:43,800
Then you're still fine.

395
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:48,440
How many steps are left?

396
00:14:48,760 --> 00:14:50,000
Can someone tell me?

397
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:51,040
I'll carry you.

398
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:54,400
Once Officer Huang hits the plateau...

399
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:55,720
...he feels like a totally different person.

400
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:08,400
I actually picked Hu Xianxu.

401
00:15:09,480 --> 00:15:10,520
Because he was in...

402
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:12,000
that *I Am Nobody*.

403
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:13,320
But I picked you.

404
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:13,800
Bro.

405
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:18,640
I wrote you down this time.

406
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:21,240
Anyway, I voted for those two.

407
00:15:21,800 --> 00:15:24,280
I think I picked Teng, Bing, and Anyu.

408
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,520
Then I definitely got the most votes.

409
00:15:26,840 --> 00:15:27,800
We're never on the good questions,

410
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:28,960
just all over the bad ones.

411
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:40,560
Xiao Hu, six votes.

412
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:42,880
Churan, five votes.

413
00:15:44,560 --> 00:15:45,880
I voted for you two.

414
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:47,760
Chengcheng, four votes.

415
00:15:49,640 --> 00:15:51,120
Good thing someone got six.

416
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:55,800
I want to know how many votes Bing got.

417
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:56,840
Three votes.

418
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:57,760
Quite a lot of people want to see it.

419
00:15:58,080 --> 00:15:59,160
Me?

420
00:15:59,160 --> 00:15:59,920
Three votes.

421
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:01,000
That's not low either.

422
00:16:01,440 --> 00:16:04,200
That's right in the middle, isn't it?

423
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:16,120
I think I put down Bing for this.

424
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:17,360
I voted for you, bro.

425
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:18,280
I really did pick you.

426
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:19,080
I put down three people.

427
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:21,360
It's the same idea as picking the outfits.

428
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:22,640
One from the Old Money group,

429
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:24,080
one from the Macho Men,

430
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:25,440
and one from the Trendy group.

431
00:16:25,640 --> 00:16:26,320
I think you...

432
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:28,280
I think I chose Churan,

433
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:29,000
Jingyu...

434
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Anyway, I picked Bing.

435
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:30,840
For Officer Huang, I forgot

436
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:31,960
whether I picked him or not.

437
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:32,840
But I didn't pick Churan.

438
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:34,440
Because I misread the question, I think.

439
00:16:34,440 --> 00:16:35,040
I thought

440
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:37,720
it meant turning into a woman.

441
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:42,040
How come my reasoning back then

442
00:16:42,040 --> 00:16:43,480
is different from what I'm thinking now?

443
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:44,080
It changed, right?

444
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:45,240
I voted for you.

445
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:46,840
Picking me makes total sense.

446
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:49,080
No, wait.

447
00:16:49,080 --> 00:16:50,160
Those three thousand of yours,

448
00:16:50,160 --> 00:16:51,240
they're all like this.

449
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:52,280
Plus those 20-odd others,

450
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:53,600
you need some like this,

451
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:56,400
or those three thousand won't stand out.

452
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:02,800
The next mission is called...

453
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:15,400
First, rule out Chengcheng and me.

454
00:17:17,760 --> 00:17:18,360
Please stand up.

455
00:17:21,720 --> 00:17:23,200
I picked Churan,

456
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:25,000
Chengcheng,

457
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:26,880
and maybe Wang Anyu.

458
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:28,360
Is this a question where

459
00:17:28,360 --> 00:17:29,760
our three names would come up?

460
00:17:32,480 --> 00:17:34,320
You picked three human shields, right?

461
00:17:37,080 --> 00:17:37,920
To be honest,

462
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:40,040
having them by my side

463
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:42,040
is deadlier than actual enemies.

464
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:46,280
Someone I can fend off for a bit,

465
00:17:47,120 --> 00:17:47,800
that's who I'd pick.

466
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:50,360
I get his logic now.

467
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:51,280
It's like,

468
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:52,360
if two people

469
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:54,480
are being chased by a big bear,

470
00:17:54,880 --> 00:17:56,040
I might not beat the bear,

471
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:57,160
but I can outfight him!

472
00:17:58,920 --> 00:18:01,200
I think that was my logic too.

473
00:18:01,480 --> 00:18:02,400
Who did you pick?

474
00:18:02,520 --> 00:18:03,920
First off, I picked Bing,

475
00:18:03,920 --> 00:18:04,560
as I recall.

476
00:18:04,760 --> 00:18:05,680
Don't say it!

477
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:11,600
He's completely lost it.

478
00:18:13,920 --> 00:18:16,360
I think I picked you two and Huang Jingyu.

479
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:19,200
Laying down a smoke screen.

480
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:20,760
Let's just pick those two then.

481
00:18:21,160 --> 00:18:22,200
Come on, hurry up.

482
00:18:22,880 --> 00:18:23,600
Officer Huang definitely...

483
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:24,160
Officer Huang definitely...

484
00:18:24,640 --> 00:18:26,160
Notice no one at the table says,

485
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:26,920
"I picked you."

486
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:28,080
No, they might be bluffing.

487
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:28,720
"I picked you too."

488
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:29,520
Right?

489
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:31,120
I think it's you two.

490
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:32,760
The two of us?

491
00:18:42,680 --> 00:18:44,280
I feel like we're gonna get crushed.

492
00:18:44,280 --> 00:18:44,640
No way, no way.

493
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:45,520
With Officer Huang here...

494
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:46,520
Officer Huang got a lot, too.

495
00:18:53,680 --> 00:18:54,640
You two, apologize!

496
00:18:55,240 --> 00:18:55,800
What?

497
00:18:56,080 --> 00:18:57,320
I surrender.

498
00:18:58,160 --> 00:18:58,960
We actually...

499
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:00,640
Young man, you're still popular after all.

500
00:19:00,760 --> 00:19:01,800
Turns out that in everyone's eyes...

501
00:19:01,800 --> 00:19:02,600
I'm such a reliable guy.

502
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:03,560
Wait, no.

503
00:19:03,560 --> 00:19:05,600
Officer Huang probably stole the whole show.

504
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:07,000
Could it be that he got seven votes...

505
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:07,600
and you got zero?

506
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:08,400
Is that so?

507
00:19:09,320 --> 00:19:10,760
Officer Huang got seven votes all by himself.

508
00:19:10,840 --> 00:19:11,320
Look.

509
00:19:14,680 --> 00:19:17,080
Even taking away the vote he gave himself,

510
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:19,440
you only have one left.

511
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:21,840
You should really thank that person.

512
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:23,280
I really didn't vote for myself on this one.

513
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:25,680
Didn't expect such a huge gap in votes, though!

514
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:29,320
For this one, I just voted for Xiao Bai.

515
00:19:29,320 --> 00:19:30,920
Judging by how the game went yesterday,

516
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:32,640
whoever teams up with me stabs me in the back.

517
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:34,880
I didn't stab you!

518
00:19:35,520 --> 00:19:36,920
But you're just way too lazy, man.

519
00:19:39,120 --> 00:19:40,680
You're no partner.

520
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:41,400
You're dead weight.

521
00:19:43,560 --> 00:19:44,440
Next question.

522
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:51,320
I picked you.

523
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:52,880
Bing and Teng.

524
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:53,840
I wanna see tough guys...

525
00:19:53,840 --> 00:19:54,680
tough guys weeping.

526
00:19:57,320 --> 00:19:58,560
Bing and me?

527
00:19:59,000 --> 00:19:59,600
How about giving it a shot?

528
00:19:59,960 --> 00:20:01,040
It can't be me.

529
00:20:01,040 --> 00:20:01,600
Come on, Bing.

530
00:20:05,320 --> 00:20:05,720
Apologize.

531
00:20:08,800 --> 00:20:09,600
Sorry, I give up.

532
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:10,440
Sorry, I give up.

533
00:20:18,640 --> 00:20:20,600
Because I just imagined...

534
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:22,880
Bing is probably a crybaby.

535
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:24,280
Not really.

536
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:26,400
I just feel he's quite sentimental.

537
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:27,640
A truly emotional guy.

538
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:29,000
Fair enough.

539
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,720
Who is currently in their Prime Era?

540
00:20:41,800 --> 00:20:43,120
Are you hinting at me?

541
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:45,440
Then I'll include you, too.

542
00:20:46,960 --> 00:20:47,600
Okay.

543
00:20:48,920 --> 00:20:50,600
You didn't pick yourself for this question,

544
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:54,680
so you must've picked me, right?

545
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:58,000
If you didn't pick me,

546
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,080
I'm gonna unfriend you.

547
00:20:59,480 --> 00:21:00,600
I probably... probably picked you.

548
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:01,680
I think I did.

549
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:02,480
All right.

550
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:03,680
Good.

551
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:05,880
Done.

552
00:21:09,360 --> 00:21:10,520
Bai, which question are you on?

553
00:21:11,280 --> 00:21:12,080
Halfway through.

554
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:13,040
Halfway.

555
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:15,920
Who, if competing with you in an idol drama

556
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:17,360
for the only female lead,

557
00:21:17,360 --> 00:21:19,840
would make you scoff and think, "Ridiculous"?

558
00:21:21,360 --> 00:21:23,440
You guys are stirring up so much trouble!

559
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:24,520
No worries, if you don't know who to pick,

560
00:21:24,520 --> 00:21:25,640
just pick me.

561
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:29,000
Prime Era...

562
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:34,880
You didn't skip me for Prime Era, did you?

563
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:36,280
What does that have to do with you?

564
00:21:38,480 --> 00:21:40,200
You wouldn't skip me for ride-or-die partner, right?

565
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:52,600
No one picked me for "Prime Era"?

566
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:04,200
They wouldn't skip me for the clothing brand, right?

